{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:28:47.146560Z","id":"c3f4359f0f69de4a846e85e9cbba4b97ca41c21f770b13494fbfdcc19bfecc15","body":{"detail":"test/platform/device/device_host_test.dart and test/ui/app_screen_device_test.dart drive DeviceHost through fake ports; nothing has run PluginNotifier, PluginShare, PluginFiles, PluginCamera or PluginLocation on Android or macOS. `flutter build apk --debug --target-platform android-arm64` compiles and the merged manifest carries ScheduledNotificationReceiver, ScheduledNotificationBootReceiver and the location permissions. Unchecked: (1) zonedSchedule with AndroidScheduleMode.inexactAllowWhileIdle fires near its time, repeats daily and weekly (DateTimeComponents.time / dayOfWeekAndTime), and survives a reboot; a force stop clears Android's alarms while device-reminders.json still lists them (Reminders.list, reminders.dart:177); (2) a tap on a reminder reaches onDidReceiveNotificationResponse while running and getNotificationAppLaunchDetails from cold, and app.dart's _onReminderTap brings the app up and runs claxHost.openRoute once its page is ready, moving the frame by popstate; (3) image_picker's camera intent works without the CAMERA permission and maxWidth/maxHeight 1600 downscale, and ImageDescriptor reads the size; (4) FilePicker.pickFile / saveFile and SharePlus on Android 10+; (5) geolocator's permission flow and 20 s time limit; (6) on macOS (sandbox, com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write added) the notification permission prompt, file and photo pickers, and share; location and camera.take answer unavailable there. Also unmeasured: a 10 MB file goes to the page as about 13 MB of base64 inside one runJavaScript string (host_protocol.dart DeviceResult.toJs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"b99b8da202734d1b2dc6eacea5081ba8796aaec6a553b75447c0b024bcd5f241"},"summary":"The device capabilities' plugin ports are unverified on a device: reminders, a reminder's tap, share, file pick and save, camera and location have only fake-port tests","tags":["v1","unverified","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:28:47.146792Z","id":"0556ac93b7d57e833328c9a62e0455b6283e1758506b400d2f4b70371f243a6e","body":{"detail":"DeviceHost._allow (device_host.dart:187) checks only the stored grant; neither the shell (web/shell/src/caps/device.ts) nor the app requires a recent gesture in the page, unlike comments and artifact.publish (caps/gesture.ts). A granted app can call location.current() in a loop or open the camera on load. A Don't allow is kept only in memory (_refused, line 53), so after an app restart the page may ask again on every launch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":187},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"ca708015e3bd8b3cd75b41f38d9c6af166bda045ef6805ecccc3c0a307250cee"},"suggested_fix":"Require the viewer's gesture (the shell's frameGesture rule) for camera, files, share and location calls, and keep a refusal in DeviceGrants until the person changes it in the app inspector.","summary":"Once a device capability is allowed, the page can open the camera, a picker or the share sheet, or read location, without the person's tap","tags":["v1","security","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.708948Z","id":"81ede8920760672ac146c5198d06ea44f1dc1b0506daa24a13effd9faa5c8b93","body":{"detail":"Failure: allow camera or location for any app, then open its inspector's Permissions: the Device row is the plannedPermissionKinds placeholder (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector_permissions.dart:86), no PermissionSource of kind `device` exists, and `grep -rn '\\.revoke(' apps/clax_app/lib` finds no caller of DeviceHost.revoke. The consent dialog (device_consent_dialog.dart:52) and contract C5 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-real-apps-design.md) promise the grant is kept until revoked in the app inspector, so an Allow is irrevocable short of clearing the app's data, and reminders of a revoked notify grant are never cancelled.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"68b1bb52f3bda987fde1b638b5403449822cd4bf62775476cbf8d796ee3dadda"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `device` PermissionSource listing DeviceGrants.list(aid) with a Revoke calling DeviceHost.revoke, passed to the inspector from AppRoot.","summary":"No surface revokes a device grant: DeviceHost.revoke has no caller, and the app inspector shows Device as still to come","tags":["v1-review","security","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709049Z","id":"1e0432d4048b960815ab10799b9281aad419758ddd64b546835ec54f4af87a67","body":{"detail":"Prompt-level consent alone lets a granted page read location.current() silently at every load, and a page that calls on load re-asks after every restart (_refused at device_host.dart:53 is memory only), so the person is nagged on each launch. The cheapest safe rule: in deviceHandler (web/shell/src/caps/device.ts) reject with CapError('no_gesture') unless frameGesture() (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:548, already fed by attestPointer in the app) holds, for share, files, camera, location and notify.schedule; and store a refusal next to the grant, cleared by the inspector's revoke (needs the device PermissionSource first). With the gesture rule a re-ask can only follow a tap, which bounds the nag even before the refusal is persisted.","kind":"comment","references":"0556ac93b7d57e833328c9a62e0455b6283e1758506b400d2f4b70371f243a6e","summary":"Recommended rule: frameGesture() in the shell for every device call except notify.list and notify.cancel; persist Don't allow in DeviceGrants","tags":["v1-review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709169Z","id":"e302b248190c6d0516c54e3df5d2747a3cb2daeb760dc774baaa76ca601e1904","body":{"detail":"files.pick returns up to 13.4 MB of base64 inside the runJavaScript source (DeviceResult.toJs, host_protocol.dart:541, JSON-encoded then jsString-escaped), which the shell JSON.parses and then postMessages into the frame; share.file and files.save carry the same size the other way through the JavaScript channel. On a mid-range Android WebView that is tens of MB of UTF-16 copies and a multi-second main-thread stall; untested on a device (c3f4359f).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"f2c0bd2430a2205e01d61ca17635e46d91c086b32bebd79cfb7a7f0cdc9d13ea"},"suggested_fix":"Cap at 4 MB for the prototype (camera results are already downscaled to 1600 px), and test one maximal pick on a device.","summary":"10 MB of base64 crosses the channel as one JavaScript string, several copies deep","tags":["v1-review","device","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/reminders.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709204Z","id":"59d989289fdb157f3528cdb73165aca8e1fe3cfd0530664ba4fb6fd3e2470b98","body":{"detail":"Nothing calls cancelAll on artifact_deleted, so a deleted app's reminders fire and their tap opens an app that is gone. _check (line 206) bounds each reminder but not their number: every weekly reminder takes one native alarm per weekday, and Android refuses an app's alarms past 500, after which every app's notify.schedule fails as unavailable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":199},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"f1357d3f6538bbca660760d46071099eb9d737ee68b19a67d0a695589ee6d3bc"},"suggested_fix":"Cancel an app's reminders on artifact_deleted (AppRoot sees the gallery events); cap reminders per app (e.g. 64) with a too_many error.","summary":"A deleted app's reminders keep firing, and a page may schedule without a count limit","tags":["v1-review","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:13.328124Z","id":"4f11429577202c458c25586495a4735a06263cee616d2a45e0a1217e0961d90a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The app inspector's Permissions lists device answers (DevicePermissions, app_inspector_permissions.dart) wired in app.dart inspectorPermissions; Revoke calls DeviceHost.revoke, cancelling reminders. test/ui/app_inspector_device_permissions_test.dart 'Device lists the allowed and refused capabilities; revoking forgets one and cancels reminders' passes (flutter test: 1302 passed, 0 failed).","supersedes":"81ede8920760672ac146c5198d06ea44f1dc1b0506daa24a13effd9faa5c8b93","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:13.329156Z","id":"48e15e1ca685ad733498ec5d932a9a72546fd93fc4ff5a7381b73bc6559edbb3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Device calls other than notify.list/notify.cancel reject no_gesture without frameGesture() (web/shell/src/caps/device.ts, 647958f22844); a refusal is kept in DeviceGrants until the inspector resets it (f1c07f346b12). Tests: device.test.ts 'refuses a call that acts without the viewer's gesture…' and device_host_test.dart 'a refusal answers not_granted, is kept, and asks again once revoked' pass.","supersedes":"0556ac93b7d57e833328c9a62e0455b6283e1758506b400d2f4b70371f243a6e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:13.331853Z","id":"3d69bd606dd023234d4c783d35f16535f672e0bdd04d239b96a83826d07a5235","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"deviceMaxBytes is 4 MB (device_host.dart) and the contract says so; device_host_test.dart 'a file over 4 MB is too large' passes.","supersedes":"e302b248190c6d0516c54e3df5d2747a3cb2daeb760dc774baaa76ca601e1904","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/reminders.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:13.332721Z","id":"dc265c5a6e6dcf6188c48902e1c65af1e0c0519a056a486b7ab45e5960d59498","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"app.dart forgets a deleted app on artifact_deleted (DeviceHost.forget cancels its reminders and answers), a tap for a missing app (404) says so and forgets it, and Reminders.schedule refuses past maxReminders (64). device_host_test.dart 'a deleted app's reminders and answers go' and 'an app keeps at most 64 reminders' pass.","supersedes":"59d989289fdb157f3528cdb73165aca8e1fe3cfd0530664ba4fb6fd3e2470b98","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:48:17.584332Z","id":"9d4ddacf0ec339c6a4a22359f9353b145d64e6a8a99268d7911e1d8d158caae1","body":{"detail":"geolocator_apple on macOS needs NSLocationUsageDescription in apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Info.plist, the com.apple.security.personal-information.location entitlement in the Runner entitlements, and a signed build (the ad hoc signature does not keep a location grant). The page gets code unavailable with the message 'location is not available in Clax on macOS yet; it works in Clax on Android'.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":219},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"cc98020f6f66fc4ec80c45699f073e7f06fea811540cf41ed46db78caf4fa46f"},"summary":"Location on macOS deferred: PluginLocation answers unavailable there","tags":["status:deferred","revisit:the owner's Apple Development certificate signs the macOS app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/location_coarsen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:48:17.584487Z","id":"3091ec0a80e5286e182b62c6fca53faf6444e37009eba59711359aa763101b71","body":{"detail":"Within one run a fix anywhere in a cell gives the same centre, so averaging learns nothing. Each run draws a new offsetLat/offsetLon, so an approximate app that records its cell over many restarts while the person stays put can intersect the shifted cells and narrow the position below 2 km. Android's own approximate location has a similar property (its offset moves slowly over time). A per-install shift kept in the app's support directory, rotated rarely, would close most of it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"f3f291073beb1aaa39b89c13045c5aab369074cc6b7cd75fe914d9d88cf7286b"},"summary":"The approximate grid's shift is drawn per run of Clax, so a page can intersect cells across restarts","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:48:17.584530Z","id":"0510ed523c680dbf322fb5e98029db5312829e6016931dd513bf9cefecd1696b","body":{"detail":"_update returns early on a fix within DeviceHost.minInterval of the last update sent. When the device moves and then stops within that second, the page keeps the earlier position until the next fix, which with the distance filter may not come while the person stands still. Geolocator's intervalDuration (1 s) makes this rare on Android; a trailing send of the latest dropped fix would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":387},"end":{"line":403},"content_hash":"c8b093cbf068059e407d5e7525a751e19217bd7aacb0bef42a9c8c52006023d9"},"summary":"A watch drops a fix that comes less than a second after the last one sent, rather than sending it later","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:48:17.584660Z","id":"df128948a8ed5afaee226130cd4ae10e32aa8e65618d5d91646c975f9b9b4fb7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c3f4359f0f69de4a846e85e9cbba4b97ca41c21f770b13494fbfdcc19bfecc15","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"d5229ec23db37c515f8330dc58978fd2bc165367f28a69ba68edd41106fc7c51"},"summary":"Since f1c07f346b12 the location port also has watch (getPositionStream with AndroidSettings), the precise/approximate request (LocationAccuracy.high or low, getLocationAccuracy for Android's approximate-only grant), deniedForever as system_denied, location_off, and openSettings (openAppSettings, openLocationSettings): all of these too have only fake-port tests (apps/clax_app/test/platform/device/location_test.dart, apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_device_test.dart).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/location_coarsen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:01:35.456169Z","id":"7d60742393c2f2b67f7feff367d0d3a9dfbe4c8690328847f2a1eb01b2af7e6f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Each app's location grant keeps its grid shift (DeviceDecision.shift, persisted in device-grants.json) until revoked or the app is deleted. flutter test test/platform/device/location_test.dart --plain-name 'grid shift': 'an app keeps its grid shift across restarts until its grant is revoked' passes (two hosts over one file give the same centre; after revoke the shift and centre differ).","supersedes":"3091ec0a80e5286e182b62c6fca53faf6444e37009eba59711359aa763101b71","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:05:34.044279Z","id":"959b975aa3f30b7297860a6550e8db9a4f6796d655f4f8d072c6030229880750","body":{"detail":"Failure: an app allowed Approximate starts location.watch while the person walks or drives, or sits within GPS noise of a cell edge. _update sends a fix the moment the cell changes (line 417, after only the 1 s minInterval), and the cell centre gives the grid away: from one fix, frac(-(lat/0.02 - 0.5)) recovers offsetLat to the 6-decimal rounding (location_coarsen.dart:33-46; a Python re-implementation recovered 0.5620124 as 0.5620000), so the page knows every edge line. The time of a cell change is the time the person crossed that line: walking north at 1.4 m/s with 1 s fixes, the edge the update implies was 1.4 m from the true latitude. A few crossings on both axes plus speed track the person; standing near an edge, the GPS jitter flips the cell back and forth and tells the page the person is within metres of a known line (their home, say). Together these break the consent dialog's promise 'Only your area, within about 2 km' (device_consent_dialog.dart:153) and docs/contract.md:3705-3709. Repeated location.current calls from taps leak the same flips, more slowly. Also: accuracy is max(2000, raw), so a raw accuracy over 2 km passes through.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":408},"end":{"line":427},"content_hash":"97ce3011379a53d0ad80356e18a1fd2480ea240c0b735b92488beaf1a4adff63"},"suggested_fix":"Make an approximate update's timing and edge carry no position: hold a cell change until the fix has stayed in the new cell for minutes and lies well inside it (hysteresis), send approximate updates at a coarse fixed cadence (Android's own coarse location delivers at most every 10 minutes), and consider Android LocationFudger's slowly drifting random offset so edges are not fixed lines; report accuracy as a constant. A test drives a fake stream across an edge and back and asserts no update betrays the crossing time.","summary":"An Approximate location.watch reveals the person's precise position each time they cross a cell edge, and pins them to a line when they stand near one","tags":["review","l1","privacy","security","location","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:05:34.044378Z","id":"50e5b651b5a896c187a110e8678d5682c322e4db325113d35c3449469c56d115","body":{"detail":"Each app's location grant gets its own random shift (_newShift, line 316; kept in device_grants.dart), and revoking and granting again draws a new one (device_host.dart:298). The shift is not secret from the page (one fix's centre gives it, see the blocker on device_host.dart:408-427), so it buys only a different grid per app. Several apps by one author, each allowed Approximate and each allowed the net, can send their cells to one server and intersect them: n independently shifted 2 km grids narrow the area roughly n-fold per axis. One app can do the same by asking the person to reset and re-allow location. The opposite choice (one shift per install) makes the reported centre identical across apps, a cross-app identifier for the install, so this is a trade-off for the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":327},"content_hash":"4481887bb19661c23b30d75ef16599fca86968a49185e525b1e10b9913088eff"},"suggested_fix":"Decide between one secret shift per install (no intersection gain; same centre across apps) and per-app shifts that survive a revoke (kept with the app, dropped only on delete). Whichever is chosen, record it in docs/contract.md near line 3707.","summary":"Per-app grid shifts let apps that share their cells narrow the position by intersecting differently shifted cells, and a re-grant draws a fresh shift","tags":["review","l1","privacy","location","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_consent_dialog.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:05:34.044471Z","id":"b016e9b5bf46d777bea871817d82275cb42aec99b19d5c2119595ec3c027bd7a","body":{"detail":"Precise is the only filled (tonal) choice (line 147), the visual default, though Approximate is enough for most pages and is the privacy-preserving answer. Dismissing the dialog (a tap outside: DialogRoute is barrier-dismissible; Back) returns null, read as DeviceAnswer.deny (line 36), and DeviceHost._allow keeps it (device_host.dart:291-305), so a stray tap outside becomes a lasting 'You said no' the person can undo only from the app inspector's Reset. Android treats a dismissed permission dialog as no answer this time, not a lasting refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"6929268a19fc389d8d9119db6e963ae10e4ba6d0114416c1d25ffadf1c19597d"},"suggested_fix":"Owner's call: give no choice visual weight (or weight Approximate), and treat a dismissal as not answered (not_granted for this call, nothing kept) so the next tap asks again.","summary":"The location consent nudges toward Precise, and dismissing it is kept as a lasting Don't allow","tags":["review","l1","privacy","ux","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:05:34.044509Z","id":"824399109a84362eaf1e9fba8276cbcdb59c400c0cc10310566d2b6d4be1442d","body":{"detail":"DeviceHost.revoke forgets the grant but leaves running watches; _update (line 410) never rechecks it. Today the revoke surface is the app inspector, reached from the launcher (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart:493), while the app screen is covered, so its watches have already stopped (app_screen.dart:484-488). A revoke from anywhere that leaves the app on screen (a wide layout, a future in-screen inspector) would leave the watch and the pill running.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":145},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"e5d9d9a72daff4c7f93bcbb31f2228fc9e9a4e9d19a095863bcf9dc2a7dcb6b8"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the live DeviceViews per app and stop their watches with 'not_granted' in revoke and forget.","summary":"revoke does not stop a running location watch","tags":["review","l1","location","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.359564Z","id":"d2d0fe87dd495297f7c1199b042f7d9b6845de7bad72442dd73824a77765d638","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"50e5b651b5a896c187a110e8678d5682c322e4db325113d35c3449469c56d115","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-15): one grid per install. A single random shift, drawn once, kept in device-grants.json under _grid, never redrawn on revoke or re-allow; the per-app shifts are dropped.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.359650Z","id":"72439523f1448bbe178730d0120c3d343027915323891fe3ffa3cff025cde921","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Implemented in f1c07f346b12 (DeviceGrants.gridShift; DeviceHost._grid). location_test.dart 'one grid shift per install: the same across restarts and apps, kept through a revoke, and an earlier per-app shift dropped' passes.","supersedes":"50e5b651b5a896c187a110e8678d5682c322e4db325113d35c3449469c56d115","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_consent_dialog.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.361139Z","id":"8bd609c19f6cb30a077aaa7bbfb56987731f7c6daed4fd044629ef9bd5d19e84","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b016e9b5bf46d777bea871817d82275cb42aec99b19d5c2119595ec3c027bd7a","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-15): no default and dismiss = ask again. No location choice is set apart, and a dismissal answers the call with code dismissed, keeping nothing.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_consent_dialog.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.361197Z","id":"e3c093afce952bd1cec220cac0031c036089569edb66a1de8a8bd112969c61fe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Implemented in f1c07f346b12: all three location choices are alike OutlinedButtons (target/flutter-app/l1/location-consent-phone-*.png); DeviceAnswer.dismissed is not kept. Passing: location_test.dart 'a dismissed question answers dismissed, keeps nothing, and the next call asks again'; device_consent_dialog_test.dart 'another capability offers Allow and Don't allow; dismissing is no answer'.","supersedes":"b016e9b5bf46d777bea871817d82275cb42aec99b19d5c2119595ec3c027bd7a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.362533Z","id":"604083c2c176e6ba4f521bb365f5ec8c2c779786348f02e9dfbb5ba414544fe7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: after its first fix an approximate watch reports a new cell only once the device is a fifth of a cell inside it (Coarsener.margin) for DeviceHost.approxHold (3 min), at most once per approxInterval (10 min), on an injected Clock. Passing: location_test.dart 'an approximate watch reports a new cell only after the hold, never at the crossing, and ignores jitter at an edge' (20 fixes alternating across an edge give no update; the update comes exactly approxHold after the crossing fix, none at it) and 'an approximate watch reports at most once per interval, and a return before the hold reports nothing'.","supersedes":"959b975aa3f30b7297860a6550e8db9a4f6796d655f4f8d072c6030229880750","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.365356Z","id":"e03eff309240e9c0a052b62dee19eee027336954b6aee167cdbe34cd905edd8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: DeviceHost keeps the views with watches per app (_views); revoke(aid, 'location') and forget(aid) end them with not_granted (_stopApp). location_test.dart 'revoking location stops its running watches at once' passes.","supersedes":"824399109a84362eaf1e9fba8276cbcdb59c400c0cc10310566d2b6d4be1442d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.366657Z","id":"8b3261d2fddf3040b92b423bb2833ecd3d2aec477c750aab4032c07db9fbee16","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: a precise fix inside the 1 s window is held (_Watch.trailing) and the latest held is sent as the window ends, on the injected Clock. location_test.dart 'starts, sends throttled updates, and the page stops it' passes (two fixes at once: the later is sent one second on).","supersedes":"0510ed523c680dbf322fb5e98029db5312829e6016931dd513bf9cefecd1696b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:31.619032Z","id":"3b3d0ca9b6d9cc4f756a26accb44b5d7f769038d80ea3a6ba134740ff11ef4f4","body":{"detail":"Since f1c07f346b12 an approximate watch holds a new cell for DeviceHost.approxHold and reports at most once per approxInterval, but location.current returns the cell of the current fix at once. A page can ask current on each tap (one tap per call, web/shell/src/caps/device.ts) and see the cell flip when the person stands near an edge, more slowly than a watch could. Keeping the last cell reported per app and applying the same depth and hold rules to current would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":270},"end":{"line":273},"content_hash":"358de7694579460ee84c1ee4f49086152945f25a35790d1abb291805772ecc91"},"summary":"An approximate location.current reports the cell of the moment, without the watch's hold","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:39:53.868899Z","id":"aa8e221af5124363edea5487ff5b8160c5c2b6361dc78850e243528c3f84fa1d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c3f4359f0f69de4a846e85e9cbba4b97ca41c21f770b13494fbfdcc19bfecc15","summary":"PluginNotifier now runs on iOS too, through NotificationHub (lib/platform/local_notifications.dart, payload kind 'reminder'); on iOS too reminders, their taps and the launch payload have only fake-plugin tests (test/platform/local_notifications_test.dart). Android and macOS reminders scheduled before the hub carry bare JSON payloads, which NotificationHub.parse reads as reminder taps.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/reminders.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:31.628729Z","id":"d253646092521cdf1174071bb3ddcb5bd326f53246f33a24d76b2d96b5a86004","body":{"detail":"test/platform/device/reminders_test.dart covers the cap, the top-up after a fire, a cancel and the launch and tap top-ups through DeviceHost.start, all over PendingNotifier. On the Clax iPad simulator, 70 reminders scheduled through PluginNotifier without the notification permission left pendingNotificationRequests empty (pendingIds() returned an empty set), so the cap could not be observed there: the permission prompt needs a tap, and no tool on this Mac can tap the simulator (System Events and Accessibility are not allowed). Still to check on a device or a simulator with the permission granted: 70 reminders leave 60 pending, the nearest first, and a launch after one fires schedules the 61st. Reminders that fire while Clax stays in the background are topped up only at the next launch or reminder tap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"9de1544ba9c2e7cfa15caf6380c85a9386d0b9dd25b1945df4f881a67bada3e1"},"summary":"iOS's 60-pending cap has run only against a fake port; the simulator held no pending reminders for an app without notification permission","tags":["ios","device-check","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:31.628802Z","id":"ecad8377db3e98890bdac10605aa27feeb797d84bdb9ae3cc455188111d6afde","body":{"detail":"PluginShare anchors both shares at screenCentreAnchor() (lib/platform/share_anchor.dart): DeviceRequest (lib/ui/host_protocol.dart) carries no rect of the frame or the element that asked, and the shell would have to send one (web/shell/src/caps/device.ts). On iPad the popover points at the middle of the screen, which UIKit accepts. iOS's page shares are to move to WebKit's navigator.share, which anchors itself.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"97f3073ecfff43bececdc42d9af2aac361ccc2fb7aede314a1427e02d67b477f"},"summary":"A page's share anchored at the frame's rect rather than the screen's centre","tags":["ios","revisit:iOS page shares stay on PluginShare rather than WebKit's navigator.share","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:40:45.917392Z","id":"4c66f56e21cb4451de326ef97297d6097a9a6de02ba5644b4fb75674796021f3","body":{"detail":"test/platform/device/plugin_location_test.dart drives PluginLocation(platform: TargetPlatform.macOS) through a fake GeolocatorPlatform; //apps/clax_app:macos_app_test checks the entitlement com.apple.security.personal-information.location in the release build and NSLocationUsageDescription in Info.plist, and a -c dbg build of //apps/clax_app:macos_app carries the entitlement too (codesign -d --entitlements). Unchecked: (1) the prompt shows NSLocationUsageDescription's text and geolocator_apple's requestAlwaysAuthorization (PermissionHandler.m) answers once the person picks; (2) a denied Mac answers deniedForever (geolocator_apple maps kCLAuthorizationStatusDenied to it), so system_denied and the System Settings toast follow; (3) under the ad hoc signature of the Bazel and Xcode builds macOS may tie the grant to the build's code hash and ask again after each rebuild; (4) geolocator_apple reports LocationAccuracyStatus.precise on macOS always (LocationAccuracyHandler.m), so an Approximate grant relies on DeviceHost's coarsening alone; (5) the 20 s time limit of current on a Mac with Wi-Fi off.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":391},"content_hash":"9452c199d94d7968f0380481814da2c750c25567aedc91f92bd2ec7adbf3e57e"},"summary":"Location on macOS is unverified on a running Mac: geolocator_apple's permission prompt, a fix, a watch and Open settings have only fake-platform tests","tags":["unverified","device","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:40:45.927149Z","id":"8b94fba86bbef7e93e9eccc74593fa71446580d963dfd8caf300ce6a9437ac3a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c3f4359f0f69de4a846e85e9cbba4b97ca41c21f770b13494fbfdcc19bfecc15","summary":"On macOS location and camera.take no longer answer unavailable: PluginLocation runs geolocator there and take is Clax's capture sheet (lib/platform/device/mac_camera.dart, macos/Runner/Camera.swift); what stays unverified on a Mac is in the concerns on device_plugins.dart:224-391 and Camera.swift:162-334.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:40:45.928478Z","id":"925c10fa2618d01a6ecec75777940408fe1faaa39b7d7a72f101984419cc6f57","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"PluginLocation now runs on macOS; the Runner has NSLocationUsageDescription and the location entitlement. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:platform_device_plugin_location_test //apps/clax_app:macos_app_test: both PASSED (PASS: app entitlement com.apple.security.personal-information.location, PASS: usage string NSLocationUsageDescription). The signed-build question stays open in the concern on device_plugins.dart:224-391.","supersedes":"9d4ddacf0ec339c6a4a22359f9353b145d64e6a8a99268d7911e1d8d158caae1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
